  "question": "Find the area bounded by $y=2x^2$ and $y=8-x^2$.",
  "answeroption": "C",
  "explanation": "Solve $2x^2=8-x^2 \\Rightarrow x=\\pm\\frac{2\\sqrt{6}}{3}$.<br /><br />Area $=\\int_{-2\\sqrt{6}/3}^{2\\sqrt{6}/3}(8-3x^2)dx=\\frac{64\\sqrt{6}}{9}$.<br /><br />Thus required area is $\\frac{64\\sqrt{6}}{9}$ square units.",
